  "bodyTypst": "The function $f$ is defined by the power series\n\n$ f(x)= sum_(n = 0)^(oo) frac((- 1)^(n) x^(2 n),(2 n + 1)!)= 1 - frac(x^(2),3!)+ frac(x^(4),5!)- frac(x^(6),7!)+ dots.h.c + frac((- 1)^(n) x^(2 n),(2 n + 1)!)+ dots.h.c $\n\nfor all real numbers $x$.\n\n(a) Find $f'(0)$ and $f''(0)$. Determine whether $f$ has a local maximum, a local minimum, or neither at $x = 0$. Give a reason for your answer.\n\n(b) Show that $1 - frac(1,3!)$ approximates $f(1)$ with error less than $frac(1,100)$.\n\n(c) Show that $y = f(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation $x y'+ y = cos x$.",
